\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Left: SPD decomposition of the paired TMS model. Right: Softmax of the paired TMS model. SPD finds the correct structure of pairing features together but does not attribute one feature pair per subcomponent. Softmax achieves the desired importance decomposition, with the exception of one feature pair. SPD was trained with $200$ subcomponents and Softmax with $100$, as these yielded the best results for each method.}}{9}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:both}{{3}{9}{Left: SPD decomposition of the paired TMS model. Right: Softmax of the paired TMS model. SPD finds the correct structure of pairing features together but does not attribute one feature pair per subcomponent. Softmax achieves the desired importance decomposition, with the exception of one feature pair. SPD was trained with $200$ subcomponents and Softmax with $100$, as these yielded the best results for each method}{figure.3}{}}
